%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Labyrinth2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551373
    - rid: 268099571011551375
    - rid: 268099571011551377
    - rid: 268099571011551378
    - rid: 268099571011551379
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d64100fc3c084684aa842f277fcb2790, type: 2}
    dialog: <font=dragonfont>niv4r3n muz fen s3v nid 1z het</font>.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551380
    - rid: 268099571011551381
    - rid: 268099571011551382
    - rid: 268099571011551383
    - rid: 268099571011551384
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: He spoke again?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Their influence must finally be waning after all of these years...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: What do you mean by that, Mr. Aren?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Atmah and Hafnar...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: The power of their souls are the only thing keeping Morokei sealed down
      here, after we unintentionally released him.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551385
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: But, if Morokei is this vocal, their power must be all but drained.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: A silver-lining for this Eye of Magnus nonsense, I suppose; we have the
      opportunity to stop Morokei before he's unleashed on Tamriel.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Atmah and Hafnar were your friends, right?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551386
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Of course they were, we would spend every day in the Arcanaeum-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551387
    - rid: 268099571011551388
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Learning new spells, discovering strange alchemical interactions, parsing
      Oblivion, and even playing practical jokes on each other.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: In fact, one day, Atmah pulled me aside and-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Nevermind.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551389
    - rid: 268099571011551390
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551391
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d64100fc3c084684aa842f277fcb2790, type: 2}
    dialog: You do not answer. Must I use this... <i>guttural</i> language of yours?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551392
    - rid: 268099571011551393
    - rid: 268099571011551394
    - rid: 268099571011551395
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Should we say something, Mr. Aren?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: No. It's for the best that Morokei knows as little as possible about
      our group.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm sure he'll remember me, but there's still the potential element of
      surprise from two unassuming dragon slayers.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551396
    - rid: 268099571011551397
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah~ ehehe...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551398
    - rid: 268099571011551399
    - rid: 268099571011551400
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Figures that the fire spirit would've returned too...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Mr. Aren, what <i>are</i> those spirits, anyway?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551401
    - rid: 268099571011551403
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: A fair question.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551402
    - rid: 268099571011551404
    - rid: 268099571011551406
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: To my understanding, they are magical constructs formed by Shalidor himself
      to guard these halls.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Their ancient Nordic appearance implies that the energy that forms and
      powers them originated from some poor Nord's soul...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551408
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Now, what makes this interesting, is that they appear to reform over
      time.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551407
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: As you're probably aware, enchanted objects require recharging once expended,
      through additional soul gems.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551412
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Which does raise the question, who would be recharging the power of the
      spirits?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Either Shalidor's magic connects directly to an Aetherial soul, rather
      than contracting out to the Ideal Masters-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551413
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Or the power comes from some other source unrelated to souls.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Savos blasts the firery wall and its corresponding spirit with frost,
      destroying both.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551409
    - rid: 268099571011551410
    - rid: 268099571011551411
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Which we should look into at a future time.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551414
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551415
    - rid: 268099571011551421
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d64100fc3c084684aa842f277fcb2790, type: 2}
    dialog: Have you returned, Aren? My old <SineText=4>friend</SineText>?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551416
    - rid: 268099571011551417
    - rid: 268099571011551418
    - rid: 268099571011551419
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5dd903fc51212df42958a6834f3e050b, type: 2}
    dialog: Sardonic bastard...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Just after Savos makes his complaints known, the party encounters some
      ghostly warriors.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551420
    - rid: 268099571011551422
    - rid: 268099571011551423
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099571011551424
    - rid: 268099571011551425
    - rid: 268099571011551426
    - rid: 268099571011551427
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
